menu "NTP Tool Configuration"

    config SYSTEM_TIMEZONE
        string "Device Timezone Configuration"
        default "UTC0"
        help
            NTP Tool timezone configuration - single source of truth for device timezone.
            Default is set for Belgium/Central European Time (UTC+1) with DST.
            
            Examples:
            - UTC: "UTC0"
            - Central European Time (Belgium): "CET-1CEST,M3.5.0,M10.5.0/3"
            - Pacific Standard Time: "PST8PDT,M3.2.0,M11.1.0"
            - Eastern Standard Time: "EST5EDT,M3.2.0,M11.1.0"
            
            Format: <std><offset><dst>,<start>,<end>
            Where:
            - std: Standard timezone name (3+ chars)
            - offset: Hours offset from UTC (positive = west of UTC)
            - dst: Daylight saving time name (optional)
            - start/end: DST transition rules (optional)

endmenu